<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Course Requirements:</p>
<p><strong>Disorders of the Cardiovascular System</strong></p>
<p><strong>1-</strong>Introduction to Cardiovascular Disease</p>
<p><strong>2-</strong>Heart Failure</p>
<p>To master the main causes and pathogenesis of heart failure.</p>
<p>To master the clinical manifestations, diagnosis, and differential diagnosis of heart failure.</p>
<p>To master the principles of therapy in heart failure, especially appropriate application of blockade of rennin-angiotensin-aldosterone and adrenergic system, diuretics, and vasodilators; and to master the salvage of acute heart failure.</p>
<p><strong>3-</strong>Arrhythmias</p>
<p>Mastering the causes, clinical features, diagnostic and therapeutic principles of common cardiac arrhythmia.</p>
<p>To be familiar with the electrocardiography features for the diagnosis of the common arrhythmia.</p>
<p>To understand the mechanism of arrhythmias.</p>
<p>4-Valvular Heart Disease</p>
<p>To master pathology, physical findings, and laboratory examination of mitral and aortic valve diseases.</p>
<p>To be familiar with the etiology, differential diagnosis, treatment of mitral and aortic valve diseases.</p>
<p>To know pathology, clinical manifestation, physical findings, and laboratory examination of other valvular diseases.</p>
<p><strong>5-</strong>coronary heart disease &nbsp;</p>
<p>To master the risk factors, mechanism, and prevention of atherosclerosis</p>
<p>To master the mechanism of myocardium ischemia in coronary heart diseases (CHD)</p>
<p>To master the main clinical types of coronary artery diseases: chronic stable CHD and acute coronary syndrome (ACS)</p>
<p>To master the characteristics of chest pain and therapeutic principle of stable angina pectoris</p>
<p>To master the mechanism and clinical manifestation of ACS</p>
<p>To master clinical&nbsp;manifestation, ECG, cardiac markers, diagnosis, differentiation, and management of acute myocardial infarction</p>
<p>To be familiar with the ECG changes, classification, and differentiation of stable angina pectoris</p>
<p>To be familiar with the complication of acute myocardial and approach of reperfusion therapy</p>
<p>To be familiar with the pathophysiology of the angina pectoris and myocardial infarction</p>
<p>To be familiar with the common drugs for the anti-ischemic and anti-thrombotic therapy</p>
<p>6-Essential Hypertension</p>
<p>To master the diagnosis and treatment of hypertension</p>
<p>To be familiar with secondary hypertension and malignant hypertension</p>
<p><strong>7-</strong>Cardiomyopathies and myocarditis</p>
<p>To master</p>
<p>1.classification of cardiomyopathy. &nbsp;</p>
<p>2.Dialated cardiomyopathy: symptoms, physical examination, laboratory examinations and treatment. &nbsp;</p>
<p>3.hypertrophic cardiomyopathy: symptoms, physical examination, laboratory examinations and treatment.</p>
<p>To be familiar with</p>
<p>1.treatment of dilated cardiomyopathy and hypertrophic cardiomyopathy</p>
<ol start="2">
<li>restrictive cardiomyopathy</li>
<li>myocarditis</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>8-</strong>Infective endocarditis</p>
<p>To master the definition, clinical manifestations, laboratory examinations, diagnosis, and therapeutic principles of infective endocarditis.</p>
<p>To grasp the etiology, pathogenesis, and differential diagnosis of infective endocarditis.</p>
<p>To understand the prevention methods and prognosis.</p>
<p><strong>Disorders of the Gastrointestinal System</strong></p>
<p><strong>1-</strong>Introduction to Gastrointestinal and Hepatic Diseases</p>
<p><strong>2-</strong>Gastritis</p>
<p>To master the etiology and clinical manifestations of acute gastritis.</p>
<p>To master the classification, diagnosis, and differential diagnosis of chronic gastritis.</p>
<p>To be familiar with etiology, pathology, and therapeutic principles of chronic gastritis.</p>
<p><strong>3-</strong>Peptic Ulcer</p>
<p>To master the clinical manifestations, diagnosis, and therapy of this disease.</p>
<p>To be familiar with the etiology and pathogenesis of this disease.</p>
<p>To understand the complications of this disease.</p>
<p>4-Gastroesophageal Reflux Disease</p>
<p>To master the definition, classification, manifestation and diagnosis of GERD.</p>
<p>To be familiar with the pathogenesis, diagnostic measures, and therapy of GERD</p>
<p>5-&nbsp;Metabolic dysfunction-associated steatotic liver disease (MASLD)</p>
<p>1.To understand the risk factors, diagnostic criteria, and treatment principles of MASLD</p>
<p>2.To be familiar with the pathology and prognosis of MASLD</p>
<p>3.To gain an understanding of the pathogenesis of MASLD</p>
<p>6-Irritable Bowel Syndrome</p>
<p>To master the definition, Rome III criteria, major clinical features, treatment of IBS.</p>
<p>To be familiar with the pathogenesis of IBS, the laboratory parameters.</p>
<p><strong>7-</strong>Gastrointestinal bleeding</p>
<p>To master etiology of GI bleeding, high risk patients, endoscopic examination, therapy of GI bleeding.</p>
<p>To be familiar with manner of presentation, resuscitation of GI bleeding patients, GI bleeding of obscure origin.</p>
<p><strong>8</strong><strong>-</strong>Inflammatory Bowel Disease</p>
<p>To master clinical&nbsp;manifestations, diagnosis and differential diagnosis of this disease.</p>
<p>To be familiar with the therapeutic principles of this disease.</p>
<p>To understand the etiology and pathogenesis of this disease.</p>
<p><strong>9-</strong>Liver Cirrhosis</p>
<p>To master the definition, etiology, major clinical features, treatment of liver cirrhosis and the management of its complications.</p>
<p>To be familiar with the pathogenesis of cirrhosis, the laboratory parameters which are associated with etiology&nbsp;and severity (compensate or decompensate cirrhosis).</p>
<p><strong>10-</strong>Hepatic encephalopathy</p>
<p>To master clinical&nbsp;manifestations, diagnosis, differential diagnosis, and therapeutic principles.</p>
<p>To be familiar with the pathogenesis of hepatic encephalopathy, and to make a relationship with the therapy.</p>
<p>To understand the etiology of hepatic encephalopathy and the diagnostic methods of subclinical hepatic encephalopathy.</p>
<p><strong>11-</strong>Acute Pancreatitis</p>
<p>To master clinical&nbsp;manifestations, diagnosis, and therapy of both kinds of acute pancreatitis.</p>
<p>To be familiar with the differential diagnosis, complications, and prognostic factors of this disease.</p>
<p>To understand the common etiology, classification of pathology and prevention of this disease.</p>
<p><strong>12-</strong>Hepatocellular Carcinoma</p>
<p>To master: diagnosis and treatment of HCC</p>
<p>To be familiar with epidemiology, etiology</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Disorders of the Respiratory System</strong></p>
<p><strong>1-</strong>Introduction to Respiratory System</p>
<p><strong>2-</strong>Respiratory Failure</p>
<p>To master the definition, diagnosis, principle of treatment of respiratory failure, understand report of blood gas analysis</p>
<p>To be familiar with pathophysiology, clinical presentation of respiratory failure, the principle of mechanical ventilation</p>
<p><strong>3-</strong>acute respiratory distress syndrome</p>
<p>To master definition, diagnosis, and principle of treatment of ARDS</p>
<p>To be familiar with typical imaging of ARDS, pathophysiology of ARDS, oxygen therapy, and mechanical ventilation.</p>
<p><strong>4-</strong>Pulmonary Infection (Pneumonia)</p>
<p>To master concept, major category, diagnosis, and principal treatment of pneumonia induced by gram positive and negative pneumonia.</p>
<p>To be familiar with properties of major bacteria species, the features of pneumonia induced by different bacteria, other pathogens induced lung infection.</p>
<p><strong>5-</strong>Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease</p>
<p>To master the definition, clinical manifestation, diagnosis, staging, treatment, and prevention of COPD.</p>
<p>To be familiar with the epidemiology, pathophysiology, and pathogenesis of COPD.</p>
<p>To be familiar with GOLD guideline and China guidelines for COPD.</p>
<p><strong>6-</strong>Pulmonary Tuberculosis</p>
<p>To master the clinical manifestation, diagnosis, and treatment of pulmonary tuberculosis.</p>
<p>To be familiar with the epidemiology, current challenges, and pathogenesis of pulmonary tuberculosis.</p>
<p><strong>7-</strong>Bronchial asthma</p>
<p>To master the definition, clinical manifestations, diagnosis, classification according to levels of control, severity of exacerbation, and treatment of asthma.</p>
<p>To be familiar with the epidemiology, pathophysiology, and pathogenesis of asthma.</p>
<p>To be familiar with patient education and management of asthma.</p>
<p><strong>8-</strong>Lung cancer</p>
<p>To master the classifications, TNM staging, clinical manifestations and therapy of lung cancer.</p>
<p>To be familiar with the etiology and pathogenesis.</p>
<p><strong>9-</strong>Interstitial Lung Disease and Sarcoidosis</p>
<p>To master the common features of ILD and clinical feature, treatment of IPF.</p>
<p>To be familiar with some knowledge of mechanism, diagnosis of ILD</p>
<p><strong>10-</strong>Disease of Pleura</p>
<p>To master the common etiology and differential diagnosis of pleural effusion.</p>
<p>To be familiar with the prevention and treatment of tuberculous pleurisy.</p>
<p>To master the classification and manifestation of pneumothorax.</p>
<p><strong>11-</strong>Pulmonary Thromboembolism</p>
<p>To master the definition, risk factors, clinical manifestations, diagnosis, and treatment of acute PE.</p>
<p>To be familiar with the epidemiology, pathophysiology and prevention of acute PE.</p>
<p>To be familiar with the manifestations, diagnosis and treatment of chronic PE.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p></font></span><b style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;mso-ansi-font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
